From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: bridge: import sample-only IOSurfaces read-only (metal2vulkan patch 0038)

Carries bridge/patches/0038-read-only-views-on-ios.patch. The render server and WebKit's GPU process texture new IOSurfaces at
every frame; each writable import cost NativeAdreno a cache clean and invalidate of all its pages when mapped and another
invalidate when let go. A surface texture whose usage is only sampled (no render target, shader write or atomics) is now imported
with Metal's private option bit 24, which the runtime turns into a read-only view of the pages; NativeAdreno pins those for reading
only and maps them into the GPU read-only, so letting one go invalidates nothing. A sample-only ask may share a live writable
import, never the reverse; a refused read-only import falls back to a writable one. Blits into a read-only import are counted and
the first logged (their writes are dropped, as Metal's are). PDX203_SURFACE_RO=0 turns it off. Landscape TestUFO: unmap
invalidate 559 -> 259 ms in 10 s, portrait 247 -> 100.

