@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+pdx203: no-copy memory of Metal's private option bit 24 imported through a read-only view on iOS too
+
+The render server textures each client IOSurface it composites at every frame, and most are new surfaces: each writable import cost
+a clean and invalidate of all its pages when the kernel mapped it and another invalidate when it let it go (landscape TestUFO: about
+1 s of kernel time in 10 s). The frontend now imports a surface that is only sampled with bit 24; through a read-only view of its
+pages (mach_vm_remap, mprotect), NativeAdreno pins it for reading only and maps it into the GPU read-only: cleaned when mapped,
+nothing when let go. The GPU's writes to it are dropped, as Metal's are, and such an import is never shared with a writable one.
+
